{"text": "Pay Karen Racy\n13-o41Gp\n\nPROJECT AGREEMENT\n\nTo: Mr. D.J. Leary\nMedia Services, Inc.\n1550 East River Terrace\nMinneapolis, MN 55414\n\nFrom: Karen Daragan\nPhilip Mortis Incorporated\n120 Park Avenue\nNew York, New York 10017\n\nDear Mr. Leary:\n\nThis Project Agreement, dated as of January 1, 1997 (the \"Project Agreement\"), is\nentered into pursuant to the Agreement, dated as of January 1, 1995 (the \"Master Agreement\u201d),\nby and between Media Services, Inc. (\"Contractor\") and Philip Morris Incorporated (\u201cPhilip\nMorris\"). It sets forth the terms and conditions under which Contractor will perform services\nfor the project described below beginning as of January 1, 1997 and continuing through\nDecember 31, 1997.\n\n1. Contractor will provide advice concerning media relations and communications\nto Philip Morris or its designated third parties in connection with national, state and local\ntobacco related issues and will serve as a general resource to be utilized by the Corporate Affairs\nDepartment of Philip Morris. Contractor's services may include, but will not be limited to,\nresearching media opporunities and contacts, pitching stories, arranging editorial and\nbackgrounder briefings and providing written communications materials (collectively, the\n\"Project\u201d).\n\n2. In full and complete consideration for the services rendered by Contractor in\nconnection with the Project, Philip Morris will pay Contractor $3,500 per month throughout the\nterm of the Project Agreement, subject at all times to the services being completed to the\nreasonable satisfaction of Philip Mortis. Philip Morris will pay Contractor within thirty (30)\ndays after Philip Morris\u2019 receipt of each monthly invoice. Total fees to Contractor for services\nthroughout the term of the Project Agreement will not exceed $42,000.\n\nContractor will subcontract the services only when Contractor cannot perform the\nservices internally, or through Contractor's affiliates, at competitive prices; however, Contractor\nmust provide Philip Morris with prior written notification of the name of the subcontractor and\nthe services to be performed. Contractor will not mark-up payments or expenses on the services\nperformed by subcontractors. Contractor will attach documentation of all third party service\ncharges to Contractor's invoices to be delivered to Philip Morris.\n\n3. Philip Morris will reimburse Contractor for all reasonable, competitively priced\nexpenses actually incurred in providing services hereunder. All individual expenses of $25 or\n\u2018more must be submitted with receipts. Expenses that exceed $250 must be approved in advance\nby Philip Morris. Total reimbursement to Contractor for expenses throughout the term of the\nProject Agreement will not exceed 15% of Contractor's total fees for services rendered under\nthe Project Agreement without the prior written approval of Philip Mortis\n\nosasszsg0z",
